    <!-- Welcome -->
    <string name="welcome_1_title">They grow up faster than the photos do</string>
    <string name="welcome_1_text">A week goes by, then a month, and somehow there\'s no picture of how they were just then. Notch keeps a door frame for each child, the kind you mark their height on, with one notch for every week of their life that has a photo or a clip.</string>
    <string name="welcome_2_title">One picture a week is enough</string>
    <string name="welcome_2_text">Your phone\'s own camera does the shooting; Notch takes in what it took. A gentle nudge comes when a week is going by empty, at the hour you usually take pictures. Then come the words they mix up, the things that will soon be gone, a second a day and the same spot every year. Everything stays on this phone.</string>
    <string name="welcome_3_title">Who is it for?</string>
    <string name="welcome_3_text">You can add brothers and sisters later.</string>
    <string name="welcome_mark">%1$d</string>
    <string name="welcome_start">Hang the door frame</string>

